{"nodes": [{"id": "changelog_doc", "label": "CHANGELOG.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "changelog_moa_2019_blg008", "label": "MOA-2019-BLG-008", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "changelog_u0_sign_bug", "label": "u0-sign / mirror-image degeneracy bug pattern", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Because PSPL's u0 only enters the model squared, a bad/shared initial guess can make curve_fit converge to the wrong-sign mirror-image solution with an artificially tight posterior that still looks converged -- first hit while consolidating two MCMC scripts and silently reusing one dataset's hardcoded guess for another; only caught by comparing against a previous run's known values."}, {"id": "changelog_wrong_but_plausible_pattern", "label": "\"Wrong-but-plausible result\" recurring failure pattern", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Repeatedly observed across sessions: neither chi2/dof nor posterior shape reveals a wrong model or wrong-sign fit on its own (OGLE-only single-lens fit to a binary event, u0-sign bug, near-miss cusp trajectories) -- wrongness only surfaces via an independent check (external data comparison, image-count geometry test, or a second implementation)."}, {"id": "changelog_bic_verdict", "label": "BIC-based 2L1S-vs-PSPL model-comparison verdict plan", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "deltaBIC > 10 (Kass & Raftery) read as decisive; if only marginally under that threshold, the documented trigger is to escalate to a real Bayes factor via nested sampling (e.g. dynesty) rather than accept an ambiguous call. Still blocked as of session 9 on resolving the 2L1S search problem."}, {"id": "changelog_collaboration_mode", "label": "\"User writes, Claude reviews\" collaboration mode", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The default mode per CLAUDE.md's guiding-role rule; explicitly overridden session-by-session for scoped pieces (quintic/root-finding core in session 3, full parallax propagation to O-03-BLG235 in session 9) at the user's direct request."}, {"id": "changelog_graphify_out_relocation", "label": "graphify-out/ relocation into microlensing/", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The knowledge graph had been living one directory level outside the project (Desktop-level graphify-out/), which CLAUDE.md's outside-folder-access rule flagged as needing explicit user sign-off; rebuilt from scratch scoped to just microlensing/ per explicit request, old Desktop-level copy left in place at the time (later found already gone)."}, {"id": "changelog_wyrzykowski_2015", "label": "Wyrzykowski et al. 2015", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "changelog_bond_2004", "label": "Bond et al. 2004 (arXiv:astro-ph/0404309)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "changelog_bachelet_2022", "label": "Bachelet et al. 2022 (arXiv:2205.07522)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "changelog_kass_raftery", "label": "Kass & Raftery (BIC decisive threshold)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "changelog_han_gould_2003", "label": "Han & Gould (2003) Galactic density prior", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "changelog_witt_mao_1995", "label": "Witt & Mao (1995)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "changelog_networkx_dropped", "label": "networkx (erroneously listed, unused, dropped)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Not imported by any script in the repo; likely an artifact of graphify's own setup in this venv rather than a pipeline dependency -- dropped from requirements.txt in session 9's cleanup."}, {"id": "changelog_mpmath_dropped", "label": "mpmath (transitive sympy dependency, dropped)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only present as sympy's own dependency; dropped from requirements.txt alongside sympy since neither belongs in the main pipeline's dependency list."}, {"id": "changelog_upstream_chi2_pattern", "label": "\"Bad chi2 can come from upstream issues, not the model\" pattern", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Session 5 explicitly names this as a shared lesson between two distinct findings that session: the O-03-BLG235 frozen-calibration bug and MOA-2019-BLG-008's mag_err underestimation -- a catastrophically bad chi2 can come entirely from something upstream of the physical model (flux calibration; error-bar normalization) rather than indict the model or the search algorithm."}, {"id": "changelog_mulensmodel_convention_bug", "label": "MulensModel cross-check convention-bug pattern (alpha 180deg offset)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A cross-check against a second independent implementation isn't automatically trustworthy just because it's 'the oracle' -- the first MulensModel comparison pass showed up to ~250x disagreement near caustics that looked like a real binary_magnification bug, but was actually a coordinate-convention bug in the comparison script itself (MulensModel's own alpha is shifted 180deg from its otherwise-documented convention). Explicitly described in CHANGELOG as the same category of failure as the u0-sign bug."}, {"id": "changelog_mass_distance_open_question", "label": "Central open question restated (session 1): tE can't separate mass from distance", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Session 1's stated central open question: PSPL's fitted parameters (t0,u0,tE,fs,fb) alone cannot give a lens mass or distance -- tE conflates angular Einstein radius and relative proper motion with no way to separate them from single-band photometry alone. Directly motivated session 2's estimate_mass() work."}, {"id": "changelog_degenerate_input_reuse_pattern", "label": "\"Zero out new params to recover old special case\" reuse trick", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "First used for lc_models.plain_flux()/plain_magnitude() (piE_N=piE_E=0 collapses the parallax terms exactly), then explicitly generalized one level up in session 9 to an entire calibration fit: fit_joint_pspl() with delta_sN/delta_sE fixed at zero recovers the pre-parallax model as an exact special case, avoiding a second near-duplicate chi2 function."}], "edges": [{"source": "changelog_doc", "target": "requirements_doc", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "changelog_doc", "target": "claude_o_05_blg086", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "changelog_doc", "target": "claude_o_03_blg235", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "changelog_doc", "target": "changelog_moa_2019_blg008", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "changelog_bachelet_2022", "target": "changelog_moa_2019_blg008", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "changelog_wyrzykowski_2015", "target": "claude_o_05_blg086", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "changelog_bond_2004", "target": "claude_o_03_blg235", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CHANGELOG.md", "source_location": null,